# 1. Use ai-standards for shared engineering rules

Status: accepted

## Context

We want every project, and every AI assistant working on it, to follow the same readable, tested,
secure conventions without relying on people remembering them.

## Decision

Scaffold and update this project from ai-standards (org `{{ org }}`, stack `{{ stack }}`).
Rules are enforced by tools where possible (formatter, linter, type checker, coverage, CI,
pre-commit, AI-tool hooks), and documented for AI tools in `AGENTS.md`.

## Consequences

Managed files are not edited locally. Changes to them go through the ai-standards repo and reach
this project through `copier update` (a monthly workflow opens the PR automatically).
